{
 "title": "Chapter 8: The Old Fear Returns",
 "sections": [
  {
   "title": "Chapter 8: The Old Fear Returns",
   "beats": [
    {
     "id": "s09i01",
     "text": "And this is where history *stops* being history.",
     "shot": "in_drop",
     "type": "HOST",
     "sfx": [
      [
       "slam",
       "w:stops",
       0.6
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s09i02",
     "text": "Everything from here on happened in *your* lifetime.",
     "shot": "in_drop",
     "type": "HOST"
    },
    {
     "id": "s09b01",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "Putin promised *stability*.",
     "shot": "c8_stability",
     "date": 2000,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "pop",
       "w:stability",
       0.4
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s09b02",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "And in the early 2000s, helped by high *energy* prices, he delivered it.",
     "shot": "c8_recovery",
     "date": 2003,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "coins",
       "w:prices",
       0.4
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s09b03",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "The economy *recovered*.",
     "shot": "c8_recovery",
     "sfx": [
      [
       "ding",
       "w:recovered",
       0.4
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s09b04",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "The state *centralised*.",
     "shot": "c8_recovery",
     "sfx": [
      [
       "pop",
       "w:centralised",
       0.4
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s09b05",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "Russia regained *influence* abroad.",
     "shot": "c8_recovery",
     "sfx": [
      [
       "pop",
       "w:influence",
       0.4
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s09b06",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "Putin also called the collapse of the Soviet Union a major geopolitical *catastrophe*.",
     "shot": "c8_quote",
     "date": 2005,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "paper",
       "w:called",
       0.4
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s09b07",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "And he was deeply troubled by what was happening on Russia's *western* edge.",
     "shot": "map:nato",
     "date": 1999
    },
    {
     "id": "s09b08",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "Countries that had once been Moscow's buffer were joining *NATO*.",
     "shot": "map:nato",
     "sfx": [
      [
       "pops",
       "w:NATO",
       0.4
      ]
     ],
     "date": 2004
    },
    {
     "id": "s09b09",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "From Moscow's view, the wall was *disappearing*.",
     "shot": "map:nato"
    },
    {
     "id": "s09b10",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "From the view of those countries, joining the West was a *choice* about their",
     "shot": "map:nato"
    },
    {
     "id": "s09b11",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "own security and *independence*.",
     "shot": "map:nato"
    },
    {
     "id": "s09b12",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "Ukraine became the *flashpoint*.",
     "shot": "map:crimea",
     "date": 2014
    },
    {
     "id": "s09b13",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "In 2014, after a revolution toppled Ukraine's pro-Moscow president, Russia seized and *annexed* Crimea.",
     "shot": "map:crimea",
     "sfx": [
      [
       "thud",
       "w:annexed",
       0.4
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s09b14",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "Most of the world *refused* to recognise it.",
     "shot": "map:crimea"
    },
    {
     "id": "s09b15",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "On February 24, 2022, Russia launched a *full-scale* invasion of Ukraine.",
     "shot": "map:invasion",
     "date": 2022,
     "sfx": [
      [
       "rumble",
       "w:invasion",
       0.4
      ]
     ],
     "quiet": true
    },
    {
     "id": "s09b16",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "Moscow pointed to *NATO* expansion and security fears.",
     "shot": "c8_views",
     "sfx": [
      [
       "pop",
       "w:pointed",
       0.4
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s09b17",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "Ukraine and most other countries called it an *unprovoked* war of aggression.",
     "shot": "c8_views",
     "sfx": [
      [
       "pop",
       "w:called",
       0.4
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s09b18",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "The UN General Assembly *condemned* it as a violation of the UN Charter.",
     "shot": "c8_views",
     "sfx": [
      [
       "paper",
       "w:condemned",
       0.4
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s09b19",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "It became the *largest* war in Europe since 1945.",
     "shot": "c8_largest",
     "quiet": true
    },
    {
     "id": "s09b20",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "Cities were *flattened*.",
     "shot": "c8_cities",
     "quiet": true,
     "amb": "wind"
    },
    {
     "id": "s09b21",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "Millions were *displaced*.",
     "shot": "c8_cities",
     "quiet": true,
     "amb": "wind"
    },
    {
     "id": "s09b22",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "Russia's own losses were *enormous*.",
     "shot": "c8_losses",
     "date": 2024,
     "quiet": true
    },
    {
     "id": "s09b23",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "Estimates run from hundreds of thousands to more than a *million* killed and wounded.",
     "shot": "c8_losses",
     "quiet": true
    },
    {
     "id": "s09b24",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "And Moscow publishes *no* full count.",
     "shot": "c8_losses",
     "quiet": true
    },
    {
     "id": "s09b25",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "In 2023, the Wagner mercenary group staged an armed *revolt* and marched toward Moscow before turning back.",
     "shot": "map:wagner",
     "date": 2023
    },
    {
     "id": "s09b26",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "In 2024, Ukrainian troops crossed into Russia's *Kursk* region and held parts of it.",
     "shot": "map:kursk",
     "date": 2024
    },
    {
     "id": "s09b27",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "text": "The *first* time a foreign army had held Russian ground since World War II.",
     "shot": "map:kursk"
    },
    {
     "id": "s09b28",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "As of late October 2026, the war is *still* going on,",
     "shot": "c8_talks",
     "date": 2026
    },
    {
     "id": "s09b29",
     "type": "STORY",
     "text": "with talks starting and *stalling*.",
     "shot": "c8_talks",
     "sfx": [
      [
       "boing",
       "w:stalling",
       0.3
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "s09b30",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "The *old* fear had returned.",
     "shot": "c8_oldfear",
     "quiet": true
    },
    {
     "id": "s09i03",
     "text": "And that's why *Kaliningrad* matters so much right now.",
     "shot": "map:gate",
     "type": "INSERT",
     "date": 2026
    },
    {
     "id": "s09i04",
     "text": "It's a piece of Russia *cut* off from Russia,",
     "shot": "map:gate",
     "type": "INSERT"
    },
    {
     "id": "s09i05",
     "text": "wedged between two *NATO* countries, Poland and Lithuania.",
     "shot": "map:gate",
     "type": "INSERT"
    },
    {
     "id": "s09i06",
     "text": "To Moscow, it's a *gate* the West could close.",
     "shot": "map:gate",
     "type": "INSERT"
    },
    {
     "id": "s09i07",
     "text": "To its neighbours, it's a *fortress* full of missiles on their doorstep.",
     "shot": "map:gate",
     "type": "INSERT"
    },
    {
     "id": "s09b31",
     "type": "HOST",
     "text": "But the real danger was happening somewhere no one could *shoot* at.",
     "shot": "c8_oldfear",
     "quiet": true
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
}